# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Package: zlib (Alpine Linux)
# Target: docker.io/dunglas/frankenphp:1-php8.5-alpine
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vulnerability: Out-of-bounds memory buffer operations in zlib.
# Rationale: Trivy scans the raw upstream base image digest where zlib is 1.3.2-r1.
# However, our production Dockerfile explicitly executes `RUN apk upgrade --no-cache`
# during the build stage, upgrading zlib to 1.4-r0 (or latest patched package).
# The built container running in production is not vulnerable.
CVE-2026-4738

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Package: github.com/go-jose/go-jose/v3 (Go binary: /usr/local/bin/frankenphp)
# Target: usr/local/bin/frankenphp
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vulnerability: Denial of Service via crafted RSA parameters in JWKs.
# Rationale: Embedded dependency within Caddy / FrankenPHP core. In this application,
# TLS termination is managed externally via Cloudflare Tunnel (`auto_https off` and
# `admin off` in Caddyfile). FrankenPHP does not expose or process untrusted JSON
# Web Keys (JWK), making this vector unreachable from external requests.
# Additionally, no upstream fix has been released for this binary in the current tag.
CVE-2026-116587

# Vulnerability: Denial of Service via empty ciphertext buffer during JWE decryption.
# Rationale: Embedded dependency within Caddy / FrankenPHP. The application does not
# configure Caddy to perform JWE decryption or token inspection at the web server layer.
# All application authentication is handled in PHP application logic.
# No upstream fix is currently available.
CVE-2026-116585

# Vulnerability: Denial of Service via deeply nested JSON parsing in JOSE structures.
# Rationale: Embedded dependency within Caddy / FrankenPHP. Unreachable because Caddy
# does not parse or validate JOSE objects on incoming HTTP requests.
# No upstream fix is currently available.
CVE-2026-116586
